Z||000003||Jefrysuko||06-04-2001||12:10 PM||||No offense spdfrek but that is the only place you can go to download PIP.  Where did you think I was going?<P>As you guy's see I was able to install PIP from the file I downloaded from another computer.  The question I still have is about downloading from my own computer.  Can anyone explane why I am not getting the normal download box and instead getting a web page with a quick time logo instead?<P>------------------<BR>Jeffrey D Suckow<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:Jefrysuko@aol.com">Jefrysuko@aol.com</A>     <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Zippy_11_sig.jpg">            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT_4.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-04-2001||07:45 PM||||It sounds like the file association for ZIP files is screwed up.<P>Under the view menu in my computer, open folder options. then go to the file types tab and dig thru untill you find ZIP files and delete the item. Make sure you only delete the ZIP filetype or you could have a real mess.<P>You'll need to reinstall the unzipping program you use to get the them to work right again. ((You need to delete the file type first because some installer won't overwrite the setting...)) ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||06-04-2001||08:27 PM||||Ogre is right. Your file associations are messed up. You can also right-click on the download link and choose "Save As".||||reg||1
